104
00:05:22,500 --> 00:05:24,970
The first one is our UI layer

105
00:05:24,970 --> 00:05:27,790
The second layer is our business entity layer.

106
00:05:27,790 --> 00:05:30,750
All our business logic must be placed within this layer.

107
00:05:30,750 --> 00:05:35,820
The third is our database and network communication layer

108
00:05:36,850 --> 00:05:45,370
95% of the code should be placed within one of these layers

109
00:05:45,370 --> 00:05:47,730
This is the first point.

110
00:05:48,140 --> 00:05:49,700
The second most important element

111
00:05:49,700 --> 00:05:53,100
that is, all these hierarchical calls

112
00:05:53,100 --> 00:05:56,280
can only be called from top to bottom

113
00:05:56,280 --> 00:06:00,360
So you can see these arrows all go from top to bottom in the UI program

114
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:01,780
call the business logic layer

115
00:06:01,780 --> 00:06:06,300
the business logic layer calls the dB or network communication layer, etc.

116
00:06:06,820 --> 00:06:08,300
You cannot call in reverse

117
00:06:08,300 --> 00:06:09,430
why

118
00:06:09,430 --> 00:06:14,250
Because this will reduce your code complexity by 50%

119
00:06:14,250 --> 00:06:18,210
Because only the upper layers depend on the lower layers

